ally sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan  firm  fairly well circumscribed mass which comes to 0 9cm of the blue inked anterior margin  and 1 2cm from the black inked posterior margin  in the medial aspect of the breast  Further sectioning reveals a firm  tan  well circumscribed nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  located 5cm lateral to the main mass  This mass is 1 5cm from the nearest anterior margin and 1 0cm from the nearest posterior margin  The remaining parenchyma is composed of approximately 30  firm  tan white fibrous tissue and approximately 70  tan yellow and lobulated adipose tissue  The axillary tail is serially sectioned to reveal two candidate lymph nodes  the first measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and the second measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial mass to nearest anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial mass near posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections of the medial mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   More lateral nodule  entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous parenchyma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node  entirely submitted  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right modified radical mastectomy  is a specimen with overall measurement of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm  which includes an axillary tail measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm nipple areolar complex with a short suture designating superior and a long suture designating lateral  The specimen is inked blue anteriorly  black posteriorly and is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm tan  firm  well circumscribed mass which comes to 0 5cm of the nearest posterior margin and 0 7cm from the nearest anterior